{{- /*
Cloudflare `_redirects` (T144). Two things live here, and both have to be
generated rather than written by hand: the identity resolver needs one rule per
material, and the canonical-slash rule has to stay above nothing in particular
but below the resolver, so an /id/<uuid>/ request lands on the resolver and not
the other way round.

Material Identity URI resolves with 303 See Other, never 301: /id/<uuid>
identifies the material, /library/<slug> is its current representation, and
those are different resources (ADR
redesign-material-identity-serialization-and-resolver). Cloudflare's file
supports 301, 302, 303, 307 and 308, so this needs no Worker.

Drafts are absent from site.RegularPages, so an unpublished material gets no
rule — its identity has never been handed out.
*/ -}}
# Generated by layouts/home.redirects — do not edit by hand.

# Material Identity URI → current location. 303, because an identifier and its
# representation are different resources.
{{ range where site.RegularPages "Section" "library" -}}
{{ $material := . -}}
{{ with .Params.id -}}
/id/{{ . }} {{ partial "canonical-url.html" $material.RelPermalink }} 303
{{ end -}}
{{ end }}
# Trailing-slash form is not canonical (ADR redesign-canonical-url-policy).
# html_handling only issues a temporary 307; this states the move is permanent.
/*/ /:splat 301
